.TH "ROARK\-ANALYTICS\-QUERY" "1" "" "roark-analytics-query" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-analytics\-query \- Run an analytics query
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark analytics query
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Aggregates metric values and conversation counts over a time window and returns one series per measure, with a total for the window and per\-interval buckets. The same query a dashboard widget runs, without saving anything. \- `measures`: what to aggregate. A METRIC measure names its metric by slug; CONVERSATION counts conversations; UPTIME reads health checks. The aggregation defaults by the metric's output type. \- `timeRange`: LAST n DAYS/WEEKS/MONTHS, a CALENDAR_ALIGNED period (TODAY, THIS_MONTH, ...), FIXED from/to, or SINCE. Defaults to the last 30 days; at most 731 days. Calendar periods and buckets align to `timezone` (IANA, default UTC). \- `filters` apply to every measure; a measure's own `filters` add to them. \- `breakdown` on a measure returns one series per value (largest 50 kept). \- `comparisonGroups` (2 to 5) run every measure once per named filter set; `comparisonMode: PREVIOUS_PERIOD` adds the preceding window's values. Values are in the metric's display units. A PASS_RATE is a 0 to 1 share; `sampleSize` 0 means no data. A query the analytics store cannot answer returns 400 naming the unsupported part.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/analytics/query
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-measures\fR \fI<value>\fR
What to aggregate: 1 to 10 measures. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-filters\fR \fI<value>\fR
Applied to every measure, on top of each measure's own filters. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\fR \fI<value>\fR
Bucket size. Defaults from the window's length and steps coarser when the window would exceed 500 buckets. One of: HOUR, DAY, WEEK, MONTH. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-comparison\-mode\fR \fI<value>\fR
PREVIOUS_PERIOD adds the preceding window of the same length to every series. One of: NONE, PREVIOUS_PERIOD. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-comparison\-groups\fR \fI<value>\fR
Run every measure once per named filter set, e.g. one group per agent. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-time\-range\fR \fI<value>\fR
Defaults to the last 30 days. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-timezone\fR \fI<value>\fR
IANA zone that buckets and calendar periods align to, e.g. America/New_York. Defaults to UTC. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-buckets\fR
Set false to return only the window totals. Optional.
